WEBVTT

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:13.210
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:13.110
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.760
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.610
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.310
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.810
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.710
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.910
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.910
...all are your friends

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.820
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.420
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:57.620
I long to fly freely

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.820
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.720
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:12.220
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:34.510
The night before their departure for Milan, Dante devised a plan...

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.310
Although Alfredo and Romeo struggled to escape,

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:44.910
...they were caught, and the ship set out into the tempest.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.010
Episode 6:

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.010
The Ship Sinks: Friendship Within the Storm

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.410
Row, dammit, row!

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.910
What're you doing, put some strength into it, you worms!

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.260
This boat is gonna sink!

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.110
Alfredo, can you swim?

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.610
The oar!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.810
You worthless...

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.460
Stop it!

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.310
Romeo!

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.110
Romeo!

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.210
Row! Row!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.610
If we go any further we're gonna capsize!

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.310
Turn back! Head back for the shore!

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.410
Keep going!

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.110
Cut the crap!

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.210
I'll not go through this hell just for you!

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.010
Alfredo, hold on to me!

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.410
I can swim. Don't let go!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.810
Alfredo!

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.910
Where are you?

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.210
Alfredo!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.610
Alfredo!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.310
Where are you?

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.710
Alfredo!

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.510
Alfredo!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:35.910
Alfredo!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.510
Alfredo!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.510
Romeo...

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.310
Alfredo, are you okay?

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.510
Yeah, Romeo.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.910
Oh, good!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.310
Thank goodness!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.460
Romeo...

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.810
Piccolo, you're okay!

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.210
I wonder what happened to the others.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.810
Someone's there.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:39.310
It's the God of Death!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.110
Let's save him.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.660
Romeo...

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.110
Mr. Luini!

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.810
Romeo!

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.110
It's the shore!

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.010
Romeo!

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:36.810
Hurry!

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.210
Get him on top of that plank!

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.810
Right!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.410
We made it.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.110
Saved.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.510
I wonder if he's alive.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:33.810
Let's take off his overcoat.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:35.610
His overcoat?

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:37.310
I read in a book once...

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.010
...that leaving someone wet in the open air after the sun goes down is dangerous,

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:48.410
He's alive!

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:53.410
Fold his arms in and out.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.410
All right.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:05.810
It's cold.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.510
I'm sleepy but I can't go to sleep...

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.310
...my ears are still ringing.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.310
Me too. And I'm still shaking.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.710
Escape.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:34.410
Now's the time if you want to escape.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:50.110
Yes, but...

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.710
...I'm going to Milan.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.210
I made up my mind when my father collapsed.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.160
Romeo...

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.110
Why did you save him?

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.210
I didn't know what to do...

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:25.310
...then I remembered my dad's face.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.110
Your dad's face?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.710
My dad always said...

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.910
"A truly strong person will neither strike nor begrudge another."

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:51.160
"A truly strong person is someone who always has the strength to be kind to others."

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:08.410
So I thought Dad would probably have saved him.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:14.660
So how about you, Alfredo?

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.410
Aren't you thinking of escaping?

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:24.610
I have nowhere to return TO anymore.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.310
Nowhere at all.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.310
My mom and dad are dead.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:33.610
There's only Bianca left.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.010
Bianca?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.010
I'll tell you about it -- about Bianca and I.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:19.910
My dad was wrapped up in his work and rarely came home.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:25.210
My mom was always sick and stayed shut up in her room.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:29.610
So we were always together no matter what.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:33.210
We grew up within a whisper's breath of the other.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:43.310
But then one day a terrible accident happened.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:45.010
An accident?

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:04.910
From that day on, I wanted to keep Bianca from suffering.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.410
And protect her.

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:08.510
That's what I swore I'd do.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:15.810
Alfredo?

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:16.510
Yes?

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.310
I understand completely.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:21.010
As brother and sister you had only each other.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:26.510
But I was separated from Bianca.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:28.810
Why?

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:42.710
It'll be light soon!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.510
I want to become an adult very soon!

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.010
An adult?

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:04.010
I want to grow up quickly and learn lots of stuff.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.310
Then I'll take Bianca away somewhere, together.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:14.810
Romeo began thinking...

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.710
...how adult Alfredo was already, compared to himself.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:23.610
He seemed to carry the weight of such dreams and hardships

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.210
...that Romeo could scarcely imagine.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.910
Hurry! Get him on top of that plank!

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.010
All right!

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:40.110
I see you're awake.

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:44.610
Why did you save me?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.010
Romeo is the one who saved you.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:50.110
Romeo told me...

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.610
...it was because he was sure it was something his father would do.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:15:02.710
The God of Death could not believe that Romeo would save him.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:09.410
It's because of Romeo that we're both alive now.

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:20.110
God Himself will surely remember this.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:26.210
Stay here.

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:29.710
But...

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.810
Wait!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:40.010
There might be other kids who survived!

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.410
If we don't look for them, they...

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:42.510
It's pointless.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.610
Don't say that!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:45.510
Move!

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.110
Don't talk back to me!

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.310
You're regretting you saved me, eh.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:08.310
Did you find any?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.010
Nope!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:14.410
Too much time has passed since we heard about the boat capsizing.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.810
I'm losing hope for them.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:18.610
How terrible.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.810
I heard the boat was full of CHILDREN!

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:22.810
Children?

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:23.810
That's right.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.810
They were being taken off by that "God of Death" flesh-merchant, Luini.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.910
We oughtta give a bastard like that a sound thrashing or two!

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:36.010
But with that storm, there's probably not one left alive.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.010
I'll go get wood.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:02.010
All right, Piccolo...

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:04.210
Time to go to the church, I know.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:07.010
Shoot! I've gotta get to the bell!

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.910
I'm a little mixed up!

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.910
I wonder where Alfredo went.

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:41.810
Where's the other one?

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.510
I don't know.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.210
Get on.

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:49.310
We're getting out of this town.

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:52.210
Where did you get this carriage?

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.010
Did you steal it?

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:11.410
Quit blubbering. Get on.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:13.110
No!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.510
What!?

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:19.010
I'm not getting onto any stolen carriage.

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:39.710
It's because of Romeo that we're both alive now.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:43.310
God Himself will surely remember this.

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:01.310
Romeo!

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:03.710
Romeo, are you okay?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.810
We could have escaped easily!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.210
But we didn't!

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.710
And now! Treating Romeo this way...

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:14.910
I'll never forgive you.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:17.260
Romeo, let's go.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:20.210
Let's go to Milan, the two of us.

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.410
We'll go to Milan. Count on it.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:27.860
And we'll keep the contract.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.710
Things'll turn out okay somehow.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.210
If we work together.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.310
Right, let's go.

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:08.210
You!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.110
So, you're the one who stole my...

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.910
Say, what is it, is something wrong?

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.110
H-Hey!

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:26.610
Buy yourself a new carriage.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:31.660
All this...!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.010
Get on.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.560
I want you to promise you won't hit us.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:56.310
Romeo couldn't understand at all why the God of Death would act this way.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:21:00.110
But, he felt that there was something...

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.110
...something deep inside the God of Death's heart...

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.710
...which had come to life.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.410
The journey to Milan was nearing its end.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:32.010
Romeo had no idea what kind of life awaited him in Milan.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:40.110
And of those friends he believed drowned in the lake...

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.510
He was certain that he would never see them again.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.810
The metropolis of Milan!

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:58.910
This is where my new life begins.

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:03.610
But Alfredo and I have to be separated from each other here.

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:06.310
I... I won't say it!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:07.610
I won't say goodbye!

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.910
Next time:
An Angel's Abode
See you then!

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:16.810
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:29.710
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:34.010
seem to end so soon?

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:38.210
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:42.410
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:47.320
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:51.220
Once again in the sky

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:58.520
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:04.120
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:08.320
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
